=== staleness-cut sensitivity (the 6h window is a judgement call) ===
      cut  contracts      ECE    floor   excess    slope
      1h        889    2.14p    3.40p    0.00p    0.997
      3h        946    2.36p    3.29p    0.00p    0.978
      6h        962    2.43p    3.26p    0.00p    0.980  <- module default
     24h      1,097    2.81p    3.05p    0.00p    0.959
  Excess ECE stays at or near zero and the slope near 1 at every cut, so
  'un-benchmarked niche markets are calibrated' is not bought by the loose
  window. The tightest cuts are the thinnest samples and their noise floors
  rise accordingly — which is the reason the default is not tighter.
